Analyzing a spinning game blindly means you cannot see the source code, variables, or the server-side environment. You must treat the game as a mathematical "black box," injecting inputs (spins) and measuring outputs (the results/stopping positions).
Here is the step-by-step mathematical framework to discover, map, and exploit developer errors entirely from the outside.
