## Phase 1: Mathematical Data Collection (Reconnaissance)
Before running any advanced math, you must collect a clean dataset. Visual slices (like "Red 14" or "Jackpot") are not enough; you must convert them into precise numerical data.

   1. Video Capture / Frame-Rate Mapping: Record the wheel's final stopping position at high resolution.
   2. Convert to Degrees: Map every result to a precise angle between $0^\circ$ and $359.9^\circ$.
   3. Establish Timeline: Record the exact timestamp of when the spin button was pressed and when the server returned the result, down to the millisecond.
   4. Build the Sequence: Create your master data matrix:
   $$\mathbf{D} = \begin{bmatrix} n_1 & \theta_1 & t_1 \\ n_2 & \theta_2 & t_2 \\ n_3 & \theta_3 & t_3 \end{bmatrix}$$ 
   (Where $n$ is spin number, $\theta$ is stopping angle, and $t$ is the millisecond timestamp).

